as we get deeper into the movie,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.080
but Scott I wanna kick off
with you, the first topic

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.210
because anytime a sequel comes out

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.770
you have two questions that are out.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.650
One, does it live up to the original,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.200
and number two was it worth the wait?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.260
We've been waiting 10
years for this movie.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.157
- Okay, well, I'll do the
second question first.

00:03:10.157 --> 00:03:11.490
Was it worth the wait?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.500
I bought the first movie,

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.570
but I don't know if I
was waiting for a sequel.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.040
It wasn't a movie where just I went,

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.560
man, let's go, two or three years,

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.240
let's have a "Zombieland" sequel

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.050
but I still had fun with it,

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.100
and here we are 10 years later,

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.800
I would say that the movie,
it's as good as the original

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.140
for what it does well with
the chemistry, with the fun,

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.610
with sort of the in-joke moments.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.300
It doesn't really expand on
it, it doesn't capitalize,

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.750
it doesn't grow from the first movie,

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.160
but I still had just as
much fun as the original.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:44.993
- Alex was that your issue,

00:03:44.993 --> 00:03:47.723
is that it does not grow
from the original at all?

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.540
- That's not necessarily my issue.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:51.600
I would agree with Scott

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.560
where it's asking me
was it worth the wait.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.710
That would imply I was waiting

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.600
for a sequel in the first place.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.900
The first one's great, it's fine,

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.910
but beyond that I was like awesome,

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.770
let's move on or let's do something else.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:07.250
Whereas this one, yeah it's
like, the issue for me was,

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.400
most of the movie they
spend separated again,

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.590
and it's like I already seen that movie,

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.830
it's called "Zombieland" one.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:18.160
I just wanted 'em thrown
together and sort of kicking ass,

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.780
but instead they're being
constantly separated

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.410
by these really specious reasons I felt.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.347
- So a more united crew
is what you were hoping.

00:04:25.347 --> 00:04:28.650
- You got a little bit of
that in the first 10 minutes

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.360
and then they just start
going off on their own again.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.720
- Yeah, and Chauncey, what I liked is that

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.740
if you ask the question was
the movie worth the wait

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.160
I think we can all agree we weren't just

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.900
sitting by the computer waiting
for the news to be announced

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.710
but I think this movie had fun with that.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.630
It started out light and fluffy,

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.790
it made a joke that there's

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.720
so many more zombie
options that you have now,

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.910
and then we rip into Metallica,

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.610
so I think the light and fluffiness

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.140
actually helped the movie.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.230
- Yeah I mean I kinda considered it

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.760
a feel-good zombie picture.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.890
I don't know if that's a thing,

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.750
but I think that totally is what it was,

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.570
and I think it was very aware of itself

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.110
that it had been so long.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.340
They were like yeah we're back

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.250
and we know there's been
so much other stuff,

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.200
but that's okay 'cause
you love "Zombieland"

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.290
and I enjoyed it, I thought it was,

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.440
I actually think it's better
than the previous one,

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.950
but then again I didn't watch it in 2009

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.070
when the first one came out.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:18.940
I watched it maybe in the last few years.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.750
I wasn't anticipating anything,

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.210
and then I actually like
that they expanded it

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.110
because I didn't like all the
characters in the first one.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.030
So it was good to kind of have
a different dynamic going on

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.130
even though I appreciated
the love of the core four.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.740
It had family vibes.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.701
- There was a lot of family vibes

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.280
in this movie and the locations we go to.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.470
I did have a lot of
fun watching this movie

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.850
and it has been 10 years
and you really feel,

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.498
the way when you look
at the actor's resumes,

00:05:44.498 --> 00:05:46.860
