00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:47.840
You see everything get done,

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.700
but it felt like as soon as
this as this movie started

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.920
we all just settled right back
into "Zombieland" from 2009.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.460
- Big time, that's what I
loved about the film the most,

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.970
is that here you have Emma Stone,

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.260
Oscar winner for "La La Land".

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.157
- [Mark] Oh there he is, there he is,

00:06:01.157 --> 00:06:03.366
the one segment before he referenced it.

00:06:03.366 --> 00:06:08.170
- But she did fit right back
into that role of Wichita,

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.370
great chemistry with
Jessie Jesse Eisenberg,

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.530
and the thing about Jesse
Eisenberg, Oscar nominee,

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.570
he created Facebook as Mark Zuckerberg

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.260
in "The Social Network", but everyone,

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.810
Woody Harrelson hasn't aged at
all since the original film.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.490
I mean he hasn't changed
his look at all in 20 years,

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.170
but yeah that family vibe
that you were talking about,

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.425
the heart, the chemistry, even
though they were separate,

00:06:31.425 --> 00:06:34.000
which I think you have to
change it up a little bit,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.440
I thought the addition
of the newer characters

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.000
also added to a different
sort of chemistry.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.160
- Yeah and I wanted to move
into that for our next topic,

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.340
Alex, because when you
talk about the chemistry

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.470
that these four have, some of
the critics have been saying

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:48.450
that they didn't really
respond to the new characters

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.283
that were introduced,

00:06:49.283 --> 00:06:51.220
that it did take away from
the core four a little bit

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.810
like you had some what I
thought were fun cameos

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.580
from Luke Wilson, Thomas Middleditch,

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.470
I thought Rosario Dawson was
a great addition to the cast.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:01.199
Your feelings on the newcomer?

00:07:01.199 --> 00:07:03.890
- I would agree Rosario
Dawson was a pretty

