00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.310
that could've gone on in this movie,

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.890
I was rooting for Rosario
and Woody the most.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:32.479
- I shipped it, I totally
was there for them.

00:09:32.479 --> 00:09:33.312
As soon as they met each other,

00:09:33.312 --> 00:09:35.730
just her being there
and his love for Elvis

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.230
and her love for Elvis, I
wanna know the backstory

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.820
and how she ended up there, like why that?

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:43.340
She has the same kind of vibe that he did

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.010
and they just clicked immediately.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.130
It didn't take long, I
totally believe the hookup,

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.280
I guess people, you know, it's zombie time

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.120
so they're looking for love,

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.660
so she found it with him,
and it was just awesome.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:54.957
- Yeah, Alex, we're gonna talk about our

00:09:54.957 --> 00:09:57.490
"Zombieland" future in a little bit here,

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.883
but I kinda like the
idea of a Nevada prequel.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.060
- Talk about how she got the hotel

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.690
in the first place, right?

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.760
Did she, was it a heist
where she went to Graceland,

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.680
grabbed all the Elvis stuff
and brought it back over there,

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.800
but yeah I would agree, out
of all the new characters,

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.220
what she brought out of
Woody Harrelson's character,

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.960
and how she was sort of the nexus point

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:21.700
where you could bring in Thomas
Middleditch and Luke Wilson.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.940
- I'm gonna just keep
the running joke going

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.943
with the "Zombieland" nicknames, San Jose.

00:10:28.795 --> 00:10:32.050
I do agree that one flaw of the film

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.710
about the characters being separate,

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:37.170
is that when Abigail
Breslin as Little Rock,

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.370
was separated from the
rest of the core group

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.300
because she hooked up with Berkeley,

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.710
that was the weakest link of the film,

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:47.707
was her storyline with Berkeley,

00:10:47.707 --> 00:10:50.304
it just didn't move the story along,

00:10:50.304 --> 00:10:54.030
it didn't resonate nearly as much with me

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.970
as the other scenes with
the other characters.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:58.620
- What I thought was how interesting,

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:00.630
Little Rock's arc is
actually really interesting.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:04.320
Yeah she would want companionship
with someone her own age,

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:06.510
and what if that guy
that she hooked up with

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.330
was actually really interesting?

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:09.440
The whole time you're kinda waiting

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.470
for them to split up because this guy's--

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.303
- He's a poser.

00:11:12.303 --> 00:11:13.136
- Right.
- Totally.

00:11:13.136 --> 00:11:14.980
- So but what if there's
actually a change like,

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.930
what if she is actually
better off with these dudes.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:20.000
- But I also thought if
you're really gonna see

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.860
how much time has passed,
I mean Abigail Brezlin,

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.970
she definitely has
matured into a young woman

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:30.880
and you're seeing her
completely different,

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.040
whereas the other characters
look pretty much the same.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.230
So, I feel like you could've
done more with that,

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:39.010
and I felt like her character's storyline

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.980
was the weakest link of the
film, but I still like the film.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:43.660
- I thought that part
was a little contrived,

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.380
but it was because they needed to get them

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.900
to go on a roadtrip,
if not we wouldve been

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.240
in the White House the
whole time, which I enjoyed.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.431
- [Mark] I had a lot of
fun in the White House.

00:11:51.431 --> 00:11:52.540
- [Scott] That was pretty good.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.320
- But I actually thought it made sense

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.090
that she'd hook up with
a really crappy guy

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.330
because she hasn't been
with anyone for so long

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.400
it's like well this guy is kinda cute

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.950
so it's like she just runs off with him

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.150
I mean that's real life
to a certain degree.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.050
- And then he ripped off Bob Dylan

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.070
and I thought that joke was so good

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:08.990
and it does make it more
convenient for the movie

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.060
that we all are rooting
against this relationship.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.160
- Totally, that's a good point.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.750
- We just wanna get our core four back.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.140
Regardless of what people may say

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:19.640
about the Thomas Middleditch
or the Luke Wilson cameos,

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.880
I think we can all agree, that kill scene

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.580
was one of the best in the movie.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.620
So I wanna talk about some
of y'alls favorite scenes,

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:27.130
if you have any,

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.440
Chauncey,
- Gotta rack my brain.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.360
- Kick me off with one of your

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:31.480
favorite scenes from
"Zombieland: Double Tap".

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.843
- Well definitely that kill scene.

00:12:32.843 --> 00:12:34.920
That was amazing.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.020
I like a lot of the White House antics

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:40.830
and then the Bill Murray scene at the end.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.270
The after credits kinda marvel style,

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.150
people were getting up,

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.710
but it was wow there's
something else going on,

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:46.820
it was an action scene,

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:49.453
I really thought that was
hilarious with everyone.

00:12:49.453 --> 00:12:50.850
- People I know that all of us here,

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.321
you've been in that junket style
situation a number of times

00:12:54.321 --> 00:12:56.060
so to see that lampoon,

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.540
I don't know how people who
do not work in the industry

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.330
are gonna receive that,
but Bill Murray's in it

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.530
so I'm pretty sure they're gonna love it.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.810
- I just thought that they
keep the Bill Murray joke,

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:06.140
gag, the running joke going,

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.470
and it does have a great payoff.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:08.590
That's definitely one of the best scenes

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:10.170
in terms of zombie kills.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:11.990
I thought the zombie kill of the year,

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.620
with the guy on the
farm in the big tractor

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.540
munching up the zombie with this machine.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.910
- [Mark] And the leaning
tower of Piza kill.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.400
- Oh, that was awesome!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.830
- Alex, you gotta love
the leaning tower of Piza.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.640
- That was good, you know.
- Come on, San Jose,

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:26.540
you gotta love it.

00:13:27.842 --> 00:13:29.100
- So what else stuck out to you?

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.680
Oh okay, well that's a redeemable
quality about the movie.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:34.400
- I think the introduction
of Thomas Middleditch

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.810
and Luke Wilson were great actually.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:38.970
I think those 25 minutes

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.240
where they're in the movie that's like--

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:43.260
- Really came alive.
- Yeah, thank you.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.970
Like really came to life there.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.270
Even the way the camera would swoop around

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.330
as they're being chased around

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.920
by the zombie versions, that
was beautiful camera work.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:54.290
This is kinda what I was hoping for

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.420
throughout the whole movie,

00:13:55.420 --> 00:14:00.420
but I would also agree with
the junket massacre at the end

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:04.430
where exactly everyone who's
sort of gone through that

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:06.280
it can be kinda numbing on both sides

00:14:07.649 --> 00:14:11.910
so just seeing this chaos
erupt from it, pretty good.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.250
- Quick sidebar so what was
the better Bill Murray scene.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:17.010
Was it the Bill Murray scene
from the first Zombieland,

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:18.890
or was it this Bill Murray?

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:19.910
- This one.
- This one.

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:21.090
- Oh, I'll go with first one.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.962
- I'm goin' first one too.

00:14:22.962 --> 00:14:24.543
- [Alex] 'Cause it was so unexpected.

00:14:24.543 --> 00:14:25.410
- I didn't expect this,

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:27.077
I thought it was very unexpected,

00:14:27.077 --> 00:14:30.287
but I thought okay he's
done, he got murried.

00:14:30.287 --> 00:14:31.120
(laughs) He got murried.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:34.190
- And I love the reference
of getting Murried.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.550
- Yeah it's like what're
you talkin' about?

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.440
Jesse Eisenberg's neurotic way,

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:42.920
but I didn't expect
that bonus scene at all

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.550
and it was a great surprise,

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.610
and also seeing my friend Josh Horowitz

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:48.710
turned into a zombie.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:49.750
- Our friend Grace Randolph

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.390
was in the post credit scene as well.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.520
- Oh yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.720
No that was, I thought that was

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.640
and listen the scene with

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:00.380
Thomas Middleditch and Luke Wilson

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:03.070
as Flagstaff and Albuquerque

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.640
basically playing doppelgangers,

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:09.563
mirror versions of Jesse
Eisenberg and Woody Harrelson.

00:15:10.771 --> 00:15:14.940
That scene alone makes
the movie worth seeing.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.550
That scene alone tops the original.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:23.330
Those 25 minutes is better
than the whole original film.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:26.090
That scene was so inspired,
it was so much fun,

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:29.040
it was so different, and it
was the peak of the film.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.370
- And what we see in this movie

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.140
is this new community Babylon

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.880
and so if we have Babylon

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:35.880
then there's probably
other communities like this

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.990
and I'm pretty sure we
didn't kill all the zombies

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.740
in this post apocalyptic landscape, so.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:44.530
Chauncey, what could be next
for the "Zombieland" franchise?

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:45.420
Are we done after this,

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.590
or do you think that there's
room for another movie?

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:49.400
Amazon had a

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.000
pilot in 2013,

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.740
could we maybe go back
to a streaming service?

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.216
Where should "Zombieland" go?

00:15:54.216 --> 00:15:55.070
- Well I'd like another movie.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:58.630
Maybe one of the couples,
I know this gets so cliche,

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.593
but one of them is having
a baby or something,

00:16:00.593 --> 00:16:04.670
and having to try to raise a
kid in the zombie apocalypse,

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.970
and I think that would
be kind of interesting.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.680
One of the great things
about the franchise

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:13.200
is that it's very aware
of itself, it's very meta,

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.630
it makes jokes, it talked
about "The Walking Dead".

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.210
So it's very aware that it might do

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:18.850
a lot of the cliches so it'd be nice

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:19.970
to do another movie like that.

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:21.130
I wouldn't want a series

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.560
because I feel like we had a series

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.140
that was very similar
to what they would be

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.480
which is "Z Nation".

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.620
I thought Z Nation was very
similar, in the same vein,

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.910
which was had the comedy,
had the outlandishness,

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:32.830
so we kinda did that already.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.090
- Alex is there any room
for redemption possibly

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.610
with another "Zombieland" or are you--

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:37.443
- Come on Alex.

00:16:37.443 --> 00:16:38.653
- I do like the idea.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:41.760
Ruben Fleischer and Jesse Eisenberg

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:44.610
did an AMA on Reddit
yesterday talking about,

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:48.050
one question was so is
"Zombieland" three in 2029?

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.390
They were like yeah that's the idea.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:52.671
So I like the idea that
there's this the "Up" series,

00:16:52.671 --> 00:16:53.890
the four sunrise, the four sunsets,

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:55.390
it's every 10 years, they come back

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:57.880
and you see where these characters are.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:58.960
In a way it is meta, right?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.650
So in the next 10 years they
can just throw a comment

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.360
on where the zombie genre has gone

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:05.210
and they just sort of keep on doing that.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.410
- And we could see maybe a child pop up

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.670
somewhere in there, Scott.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.220
- Here's what I wanna see
in "Zombieland" three.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.750
- Pitch to the other
three cities on the panel.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:17.140
- I thought "Zombieland: Double
Tap" it was a worthy sequel,

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:20.150
not necessarily a superior one.

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:22.860
I loved it for what it was, okay,

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.700
but if you're going to
do a "Zombieland" three,

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:26.950
just go for it.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:30.010
Really Just pull out all
the stops and go for it.

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:34.410
Now when I think of the great
movie sequels of all time,

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.360
I mean sure there's "Godfather II",

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.927
there's "Star Trek II: The Wrath of Khan",

00:17:38.927 --> 00:17:41.210
"Spider-Man 2"
- "Secret of the Ooze".

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:43.507
- Listen, nothing is better than

00:17:43.507 --> 00:17:46.167
"Gremlins 2: The New Batch".

00:17:46.167 --> 00:17:47.428
- I knew you were gonna

00:17:47.428 --> 00:17:49.730
work the new batch in.
- Gremlins 2,

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:53.760
was so great because it was a
spoof of the original movie.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.930
It made fun of the original film.

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.700
It pulled out all the stops.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.370
If you've never seen "Gremlins 2",

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:02.960
which came out July 2nd, 1990,
the same day as "Dick Tracy",

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:05.760
it is a superior sequel in
every sense of the word,

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:10.760
and it just was a wild, wacky,
crazy, really awesome sequel.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.210
So that's what I wanna see
for "Zombieland" three,

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.140
just go for it.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:17.280
There was a little bit of meta stuff.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:18.970
Like there was a joke
about "Walking Dead",

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.630
but really just have fun with it.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:24.560
Maybe "Zombieland" three is about

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.193
the filming of "Zombieland" three.

00:18:27.193 --> 00:18:30.854
- That is meta on top of meta.
- That's what I want to see.

00:18:30.854 --> 00:18:33.917
- Reality TV?
- Do something different.

00:18:33.917 --> 00:18:36.310
- Reality TV with zombies
I can actually buy into.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:39.550
That's a meta sandwich and
we might be here for it.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:42.000
More "Zombieland" in some
capacity is the consensus

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.530
that I'm getting from my panel

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.380
who by the way today was terrific.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:48.020
Thank you to my guests
Scott, Chauncey, and Alex

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.587
for joining me here today to talk about

00:18:49.587 --> 00:18:51.230
"Zombieland: Double Tap"

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.480
and I would remind everybody
out there watching right now.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.190
We have some really good
news here at Rotten Tomatoes,

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.350
we have our first book!

